    {
      "id": "kBN5ndYEcTzfLu9r0U4YQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10615.248237536984,
      "y": -2501.545035497147,
      "width": 6781.057381465517,
      "height": 256.5805495689655,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e2e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1376444214,
      "version": 37,
      "versionNonce": 347902698,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786391839416,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "⚠  KEY ARCHITECTURAL NOTES:\n  1. WEBSOCKET SCALING (Phase 1 limit): WS sockets owned by Master event loop. Workers do NOT handle WS connections.\n     10,000 concurrent WS = Master event loop saturated. Fix (Phase 2): worker.send(rawSocket) → workers own WS.\n\n  2. RATE LIMITER is IN-MEMORY per worker. Each worker process has its own Map<IP,count>. For distributed rate limiting → use Redis.\n\n  3. SERVICE REGISTRY is IN-MEMORY. Dynamic services must re-register after proxy restart. Production: use Consul/etcd.\n\n  4. FIX#3 (HTTP Agent): httpAgent + httpsAgent created ONCE at worker module level. Previously broken (created per-request, no pooling).\n\n  5. FIX#4 (HTTPS upstream): Worker checks url.protocol → http.request() or https.request(). WS checks wss:// → tls.connect().",
      "fontSize": 25.873668864097365,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 10,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "⚠  KEY ARCHITECTURAL NOTES:\n  1. WEBSOCKET SCALING (Phase 1 limit): WS sockets owned by Master event loop. Workers do NOT handle WS connections.\n     10,000 concurrent WS = Master event loop saturated. Fix (Phase 2): worker.send(rawSocket) → workers own WS.\n\n  2. RATE LIMITER is IN-MEMORY per worker. Each worker process has its own Map<IP,count>. For distributed rate limiting → use Redis.\n\n  3. SERVICE REGISTRY is IN-MEMORY. Dynamic services must re-register after proxy restart. Production: use Consul/etcd.\n\n  4. FIX#3 (HTTP Agent): httpAgent + httpsAgent created ONCE at worker module level. Previously broken (created per-request, no pooling).\n\n  5. FIX#4 (HTTPS upstream): Worker checks url.protocol → http.request() or https.request(). WS checks wss:// → tls.connect().",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "index": "b5k",
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
